      "refersTo": "tool-panel",
      "description": "White fixed-width sidebar preview with the actual information-row alignment and section divider. The live WPF panel uses an outer vertical ScrollViewer at minimum window height.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-tool-panel\"><h3>动作信息</h3><strong class=\"ds-file\">008b.bvh</strong><dl><dt>帧数</dt><dd><strong>513</strong></dd><dt>采样率</dt><dd>60 fps</dd><dt>关节 / 通道</dt><dd>18 / 57</dd></dl><hr/><h3>播放速度</h3></section>",
      "css": ".ds-tool-panel{width:240px;padding:18px 19px;background:#FFFFFF;border-radius:10px;color:#172438;font:13px \"Microsoft YaHei UI\",\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif}.ds-tool-panel h3{font-size:14px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 9px}.ds-file{display:block;margin-bottom:9px}.ds-tool-panel dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;grid-auto-rows:23px;margin:0 0 2px}.ds-tool-panel dt{color:#526278}.ds-tool-panel dd{text-align:right;margin:0}.ds-tool-panel hr{height:1px;border:0;background:#E5EAF1;margin:8px 0 13px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Playback Transport",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "playback-panel",
      "description": "Transport preview retains a blue text-and-icon play command, quiet framing controls, and a monospace timecode. The live timeline is a native WPF Slider.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-transport\"><div class=\"ds-transport-title\"><strong>播放时间轴</strong><span>帧 101 / 513</span></div><div class=\"ds-transport-controls\"><button class=\"ds-button ds-step\" aria-label=\"停止并回到首帧\"><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 12\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M0 0H12V12H0Z\"/></svg></button><button class=\"ds-button ds-play\"><svg width=\"11\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 11 14\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M0 0V14L11 7Z\"/></svg><span>播放</span></button><span class=\"ds-timecode\">00:01.67 / 00:08.55</span></div></section>",
      "css": ".ds-button{font-family:\"Microsoft YaHei UI\",\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:400;min-height:36px;padding:9px 13px;border:1px solid #D7DEE9;border-radius:7px;cursor:pointer;color:#172438;background:#FFFFFF}.ds-button:hover{opacity:.8}.ds-button:active{opacity:.6}.ds-button:focus-visible{outline:none;border-color:#3F82F4;border-width:2px}.ds-button:disabled{opacity:.4;cursor:default}.ds-transport{padding:12px 18px;border-radius:10px;background:#FFFFFF;color:#172438;font:13px \"Microsoft YaHei UI\",\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif}.ds-transport-title{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;height:25px}.ds-transport-title span{color:#526278;font-size:12px}.ds-transport-controls{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px}.ds-step{padding:8px 11px;color:#526278}.ds-play{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:9px;min-width:96px;background:#245CD7;border-color:#245CD7;color:#FFFFFF}.ds-timecode{margin-left:20px;font:13px Consolas,monospace}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Skeleton Viewport",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "skeleton-viewport",
      "description": "Context preview of the WPF 3D observation field and its semantic legend. The SVG is only a compact documentation schematic; the app renders shared frozen 3D meshes with lighting.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-scene\"><h3>008b.bvh</h3><p class=\"ds-scene-state\"><i></i>已暂停 · 空格键开始播放</p><svg class=\"ds-skeleton\" viewBox=\"0 0 160 200\" width=\"160\" height=\"200\" aria-label=\"骨骼示意\"><g fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path stroke=\"#DEE7F2\" d=\"M80 18V90L65 112M80 90L95 112\"/><path stroke=\"#54D8DA\" d=\"M80 50L57 62L48 102L53 139M65 112L61 151L65 190\"/><path stroke=\"#FFBE74\" d=\"M80 50L103 62L112 102L107 139M95 112L99 151L95 190\"/></g><g fill=\"#DEE7F2\"><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"18\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"50\" r=\"4\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"90\" r=\"6\"/></g><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"112\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#8DFFAE\"/></svg><div class=\"ds-legend\"><span><i class=\"ds-left\"></i>左侧</span><span><i class=\"ds-right\"></i>右侧</span><span><i class=\"ds-center\"></i>中轴</span></div><p class=\"ds-scene-help\">左键拖动旋转 · 滚轮缩放 · 右键拖动平移</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-scene{width:380px;padding:18px 20px 19px;background:#111E30;color:#F1F6FF;border-radius:12px;font-family:\"Microsoft YaHei UI\",\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif}.ds-scene h3{font-size:17px;font-weight:600;margin:0}.ds-scene-state{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;margin:7px 0 0;color:#B5C3D8;font-size:12px}.ds-scene-state i{width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:#8B9AB0}.ds-skeleton{display:block;margin:0 auto 8px}.ds-legend{display:flex;gap:16px;color:#C1CEDF;font-size:11px}.ds-legend span{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px}.ds-legend i{width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%}.ds-left{background:#54D8DA}.ds-right{background:#FFBE74}.ds-center{background:#DEE7F2}.ds-scene-help{margin:8px 0 0;color:#A6B8D0;font-size:11px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Motion Workbench",
    "overview": "BVH Player is a quiet, precise Windows tool for inspecting skeletal motion. The dark observation field gives the moving skeleton priority; white tool surfaces make file facts, playback choices, and hierarchy easy to scan. The phrase above describes the finished implementation rather than a new visual direction.\n\nThe interface uses Chinese task labels, a compact desktop type scale, and familiar WPF controls. Blue identifies commands and adjustable progress. Cyan, warm orange, pale ivory, and mint belong to the skeletal data, where color distinguishes body sides and the inspected joint.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A dark 3D observation field beside light, flat tool surfaces.",
      "A compact Chinese interface with visible playback controls and keyboard hints.",
      "One blue UI action color, separated from semantic skeleton colors.",
      "Fixed desktop structure with a scrollable tool panel at the minimum window size.",
      "Native WPF interaction, focus, selection, and accessibility conventions."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Command and Data Rule",
        "body": "Use blue for UI commands and progress. Reserve the cyan, amber, ivory, and mint data colors for the skeleton and its legend.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Native Type Rule",
        "body": "Preserve the Chinese UI font and inherited WPF sizing. Use Consolas only for the timeline timecode.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Stable Workspace Rule",
        "body": "Keep the tool panel fixed in width and let its content scroll at the minimum window size. Preserve visible playback controls while the scene takes the remaining width and height.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Tools Rule",
        "body": "Keep the 2D controls and panels flat. Use scene lighting for the skeleton's volume.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do preserve the light tool panels and dark viewport as separate visual roles.",
      "Do use the single blue action color for commands and progress, and use skeleton colors only for their data meaning.",
      "Do treat all interface measurements as WPF DIP and preserve native text scaling and layout rounding.",
      "Do keep the bottom playback controls visible and allow the fixed-width sidebar to scroll at the minimum window size.",
      "Do preserve keyboard focus, native checkbox and tree behavior, vector icons, tooltips, and automation names.",
      "Do reuse and freeze shared 3D meshes and materials; animate transforms instead of rebuilding geometry."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add decorative shadows or hover lift to the flat tool surfaces.",
      "Don't introduce a mobile breakpoint or collapse the sidebar based on these desktop captures.",
      "Don't replace WPF system tree selection or checkbox styling with invented fixed states.",
      "Don't describe the sidebar as fully visible without scrolling at the minimum size.",
      "Don't promote world-space skeleton radii or screenshot pixels into interface DIP tokens.",
      "Don't treat the sidecar's HTML/CSS previews as application source or a replacement for native WPF controls."
    ]
  }
}

